A||||1||BENGAL4||BLEEDING SLAVE CYLINDER
Z||000000||BENGAL4||07-28-99||02:32 PM||||After I install my new master cylinder, I plan on bleeding the system the v8 Archie way. My question is, where is the best location to bleed the slave cylinder? Under the car or thru the engine compartment? If anyone has done this Archie's way, please give me some pointers.<p>Thanks,<p><br>Bill<br>
Z||000001||G25C||07-29-99||12:14 AM||||I replaced my master and slave cylinder and bled it the v8archie way.  To bleed the slave cylinder i removed the rubber air duct so that i could see the slave and then i bled it by leaning over the side of my Fiero from the top (87 GT) the only thing i wasnt paying attention to was that i leaned a little close to the back quarter glass and made a spider web crack in it from leaning on it.<p>also.  I used a flat head screw drive to put into the groove of the slave push rod to give me leverage to bore it back into the slave cylinder (be careful not to rip the boot with the screw driver.).<p>i would say the best way is from the top
